@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-06-09

Feature: Disable Endpoint Command
  "CLI handler for mason disable: stop one endpoint from resolving."

  Provides:
    - cli.newDisableCommand @source("symbol:newDisableCommand")
    - cli.defaultDisableRun @source("symbol:defaultDisableRun")
    - cli.renderEndpoint @source("symbol:renderEndpoint")

  Consumes:
    - links.Service.Disable
    - cli.resolveTarget
    - cli.newRemoteStack
    - output.WriteJSON

  Invariants:
    - Human output MUST distinguish changed vs already-disabled no-ops
    - Quiet mode MUST emit no stdout on success
    - JSON output MUST use the stable endpointJSON shape under output.Success

  Scenario (happy-path): Disable endpoint
    Given Disable changes state
    When the command completes
    Then stdout reports Disabled <ref>

  Scenario (negative): Disable failure
    Given Disable returns an error
    When the command runs
    Then emitError renders the failure
